{
  "name": "What to Do Immediately After Storm Damage Hits Your Home",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "It’s a nightmare scenario: a storm tears through, leaving damage in its wake. Your home is hit, and you’re probably wondering, “What now?” First things first, safety is paramount. Make sure everyone is okay and avoid any immediate hazards like downed power lines or areas with active leaks. Once it’s safe, the next crucial step is to document everything. Seriously, take a ton of photos and videos of all the damage before you touch a thing. This evidence is going to be incredibly important for your insurance claim. Don't forget to contact your insurance provider as soon as you can to report the damage. They'll guide you on their specific process, but having your documentation ready will really speed things up. After that, it’s about preventing further damage, maybe by temporarily covering a broken window or a leaking roof if it’s safe to do so. But remember, these are temporary fixes, not permanent solutions. For comprehensive and lasting repairs, especially if there's structural concern or water intrusion, getting a professional like HH Remodeling LLC involved early on is a smart move. We can assess the full scope and help get your home back to normal.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
